WEBVTT

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:07.375
The review opens right in Claude Code, beside the chat.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:17.125
Comment on any line, and blueprint takes it into the next revision.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:24.325
Reviews live where the team already reads docs.

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:28.055
Every review opens with a picture of the change.

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:34.100
The change splits into pull requests, stacked or side by side.

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:38.825
Approve the plan, and start each group from the pane.

00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:48.025
Blueprint can also draw the repo as a map.

00:00:48.430 --> 00:00:51.830
Here, one schema change in jambo ripples out.

00:00:52.135 --> 00:00:57.035
Drift follows imports, with a chance and a confidence for each capability.

00:00:57.641 --> 00:01:00.791
Further away, it's only possibly affected.

00:01:01.393 --> 00:01:04.568
And every scenario lists the tests that claim it.

00:01:05.498 --> 00:01:09.248
On every pull request, CI says which specs to check.

00:01:13.167 --> 00:01:16.642
And which docs outside the repo may need an update.

00:01:17.247 --> 00:01:20.722
Specs and code stay honest, in both directions.
